{"abstract":[{"text":"A minimum cycle basis (de Pina 1995): ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeCount - vertexCount + c","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cycles, for c","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"components, independent over GF(2) and spanning the cycle space, with the fewest edges in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"total of any such basis. Self-loops and parallel edges are supported: a loop is a cycle of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its own, and two copies of an edge form a cycle of length 2. Each cycle starts at its least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order and leaves it through the lesser of its two edges there; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cycles come in nondecreasing length, then by their edge positions. Ties between equally","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"short cycles are broken by the rows’ order.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Cycles","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"minimumCycleBasis()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumCycleBasis"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cycle","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":">]","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"MinimumCycl